- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/guide/semantic-stage-two
  route: guide/semantic-stage-two
  title: 'Next stage: semantic map and reviewed journeys'
  type: Research navigation
  description: 26 individually authored concepts, 15 source-backed semantic proposals, a
    capital-disregard review candidate and expanded staff/persona journeys. Content freeze 24
    September; seminar 30 September.
  generated:
    by: process:codex-semantic-stage-two
    at: '2026-09-15T16:55:18.464057Z'
  observedAt: '2026-09-15T16:55:18.464057Z'
  status: draft
  authority: project-authored next-stage research
  tags:
  - start here
  - semantic map
  - next stage
  - seminar
  references:
  - term/capital-disregards
  - rule-candidate/capital-disregard-sequence
  - question/stage2-001
  - question/stage2-002
  - question/stage2-003
  - question/stage2-004
  - question/stage2-005
  - question/stage2-006
  - resource/okf-uk-legislation
  - resource/cpag-welfare-benefits-handbook
  - resource/full-dmg-collection
  - resource/advice-for-decision-making
  - resource/universal-credit-eligibility
  body: "# Next stage: semantic map and reviewed journeys\n\nThe first semantic pilot adds explicit relationships
    to individual concept files. All are unreviewed proposals supported by exact captured DWP passages.
    No rule is executable and no staff approval is implied.\n\n[Read the semantic map and evidence register](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/semantic-map.md).
    [Inspect the status, gaps and delivery plan](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/docs/next-stage/README.md).\n\
    \nStart with the capital-disregard candidate and its evidence, duration and assessment-sequence links.
    Compare the projected user questions with the missing evidence and review requirements. CPAG contents
    widen topic discovery only; the handbook text and its legal analysis are not present.\n\nFull DMG
    is a separate acquisition target: 331 PDFs in the metadata census, of which 36 are currently acquired.
    ADM has a separate 182-PDF census. The seminar website and personal-AI/audio connection remain feasibility
    work until actual tool calls and room rehearsal pass."
